<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palden Thondup Namgyal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1923–1982</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palden Thondup Namgyal was the twelfth and last Chogyal of Sikkim, reigning from 1963. His wish for more independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, while discontent grew among the Nepali-speaking majority, led to unrest in the early 1970s. In 1975 Indian troops disarmed his guard, a referendum abolished the monarchy and Sikkim became a state of India. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> in 1982.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palden-thondup-namgyal.jpg" alt="Palden Thondup Namgyal" width="320" height="532" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alice S. Kandell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palden_Thondup_Namgyal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
